**SD-Q2: where live NFL game events come from.** This is the next open decision; the backend shape, the matching logic and the demo script all depend on it. Issue #1 already settles that replay or simulated input is allowed if it is clearly labeled. What is still open is the live source.

**Recommendation: a Sportradar NFL 30-day self-serve trial, with recorded games replayed for the demo.**
- Its data is official and licensed, and the trial carries the same data as production ([Sportradar](https://developer.sportradar.com/getting-started/docs/your-account)). That gives real player IDs for matching against Yahoo, plus scoring corrections.
- It is self-serve, so it can be running before the Thursday 10/15 and Sunday 10/18 tests.

**Tradeoffs:**
- **Call budget may be too small.** One Sportradar page caps the trial at 1,000 calls total at 1 per second; another says 15,000. At 1,000, one full game polled every 10 seconds would not fit. All games share one ingestion, so the budget is per account, not per viewer.
- **Evaluation only.** The trial is meant for evaluation, not production use.
- **You must register.** The trial is a credential, which is owner-only.

